:: StoryTitle
Literature Review Scenario

:: StoryInit [script]
<<set $scenarioFeedback = []>>

:: Start
<p>You are beginning a literature review for a public health module.</p><p>Your task is to move from a broad topic to a defensible review question.</p><div class="scenario-action">[[Define the question first->Focused Question]]</div><div class="scenario-action">[[Start searching immediately->Search Too Soon]]</div>

:: Focused Question
<p>You decide to clarify the review question before searching.</p><p>A focused question will help you identify relevant evidence.</p><!-- Unsupported directive retained: YouTubeEmbed :: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yt3e8Ng0mf0 --><!-- Unsupported directive retained: PanoptoEmbed :: https://lshtm.cloud.panopto.eu/Panopto/Pages/Viewer.aspx?id=d19ba573-9ad1-480b-95db-b3ed01014aab --><div class="scenario-action">[[Develop a search strategy->Search Strategy]]</div>

:: Search Too Soon
<p>You begin searching immediately and find many inconsistent papers.</p><p>The topic is still too broad.</p><div class="scenario-action">[[Go back and define the question->Focused Question]]</div>

:: Search Strategy
<p>You identify key concepts, keywords and possible databases.</p><div class="scenario-action">[[Search PubMed and Scopus->Evidence Search]]</div>

:: Evidence Search
<p>You locate a collection of potentially relevant studies.</p><div class="scenario-action">[[Screen titles and abstracts->Screening]]</div>

:: Screening
<p>Some studies are clearly relevant while others should be excluded.</p><div class="scenario-action">[[Apply inclusion and exclusion criteria->Critical Appraisal]]</div>

:: Critical Appraisal
<p>You assess study quality, bias and methodological rigour.</p><div class="scenario-action">[[Synthesize findings->Synthesis]]</div>

:: Synthesis
<p>You identify themes, patterns and gaps across the evidence.</p><div class="scenario-action">[[Write conclusions->Conclusion]]</div>

:: Conclusion
<p>You produce a transparent and evidence-informed literature review.</p><p>End of scenario.</p>
